{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Held-out GREEN exposed an incomplete repair at the same mechanism in production code: after all fixture-owned implicit bare calls were made explicit, the strict-policy oracle advanced into infra/scripts/prepare_reclaim_backup.py::_verify_restore and failed at its throwaway restore.git. The script initializes restore.git as bare, then routes fetch and rev-parse through the shared worktree-oriented run_git helper, which uses git -C and is rejected by safe.bareRepository=explicit. This is not a new root cause: it is the construct-sweep sibling previously masked by fixture setup failure. Caller sweep is local: the throwaway repository is owned only inside _verify_restore; normal repo operations elsewhere must remain on run_git. Expected repair: a narrow explicit --git-dir helper for only restored, preserving bundle refs, exact OID comparison, checked failure propagation, and temporary-directory cleanup. File impact expanded to include the script; the held-out oracle was removed again before the continued blind repair."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787098703069961001,"uuid":"9fe087e3-7acf-4886-a653-c1abfdc90100"}